{
  "id": "resistance_vs__resistivity",
  "title": "Resistance vs. Resistivity",
  "description": "Calculate electrical resistance of a conductor based on resistivity, length, and cross-sectional area using the formula R = ρL/A",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "resistance_calculator",
      "content": "## Resistance Calculator\n\nCalculate the resistance of a conductor using the formula R = ρL/A, where:\n- **ρ (rho)** = resistivity of the conductor material (Ω m)\n- **L** = length of conductor (m)\n- **A** = cross-sectional area of conductor (m²)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "resistivity",
          "label": "Resistivity (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Ω m",
          "defaultValue": 1.724e-8
        },
        {
          "id": "length",
          "label": "Length (L)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "cross_sectional_area",
          "label": "Cross-sectional Area (A)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m²",
          "defaultValue": 0.00000104
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "resistance",
          "label": "Resistance (R)",
          "formula": "inputs.resistivity * inputs.length / inputs.cross_sectional_area",
          "unit": "Ω",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
